        "text_YicBRb": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h3>Sensitive skin</h3>\n<p>Characterised by stinging, burning, itching, tingling or tightness from triggers that wouldn’t normally cause discomfort. Skin may appear normal, or have visible redness.<sup>1</sup></p>\n<h3>Reactive skin</h3>\n<p>Skin which commonly responds quickly to internal or external triggers.</p>\n<h3>Redness-prone skin</h3>\n<p>Skin which is more likely to develop visible flushing or areas of persistent redness.</p>\n<p>These can occur on their own or together, and may be linked to changes in skin barrier function and heightened neurosensory reactivity.<sup>2,3</sup></p>",
